    "turn_text": "me, that's very reflective of a very fluid process. As someone who is involved in the fluidity of that, what can you share in terms of perspective on the direction this bill was going and why, ultimately, I gather from your comments, you were planning to support it. Oh, yeah. I mean, I, but I waited, Walter, I, you know, the president had asked me to support the bill. And I told them that I would give it a fair consideration, but I wanted to see the final bill. I don't know how anybody commits to something before they see the final product. And, you know, it's kind of a rookie mistake, I think, for some people to walk out of, for instance, the Energy and Commerce Committee and say, hey, I'm going to support this or I voted for it because it has X, Y and Z in it. Well, you don't know how it's going to look when it's all done. And",
